% Error Handling
- Return `(False, "gh CLI not found...", 0.0, "")` if `gh` command not available
- Return `(False, "Invalid GitHub issue URL: {url}", 0.0, "")` if URL parsing fails
- Return `(False, "Failed to fetch issue: {error}", 0.0, "")` if GitHub API fails
- Return a closed ambiguity-selection failure when unresolved candidates receive an empty, malformed, duplicate, or invented selection; never turn that response into a no-op
- Return `(False, "PDD_CHANGED_MODULES contained unresolved module targets: [<targets>]", cost, provider)` if `PDD_CHANGED_MODULES` was non-empty and any parsed entry is rejected before dry-run by the closed architecture-backed resolver (including runtime templates, unknown entries, or ambiguous bare leaves)
- Return `(False, "No valid modules to sync (all basenames were invalid: ...)", cost, provider)` if all basenames fail validation
- Return `(False, "Dry-run validation failed:\n{details}", cost, provider)` if dry-run validation fails
- Return `(True, "Dry run complete: N module(s) would sync: ...", cost, provider)` when `dry_run=True` and at least one module remains after fingerprint filtering
- Return `(True, "All modules are already synced — nothing to do.", cost, provider)` if fingerprint check filters all modules
- Return `(True, "All modules are already synced — nothing to do.", cost, provider)` if the runtime-LLM-template filter (Req 9, Req 10, or dry-run step 0) removes every selected basename. Issues that touch only runtime `*_LLM.prompt` templates are a successful no-op because those templates are already consumed directly by their owning code modules and there is nothing to regenerate. Do not invoke `pdd sync` or the LLM dry-run fallback in this case.
- Post error comment on GitHub issue when LLM fails, basenames invalid, or dry-run fails (if `use_github_state` is True)
- Every `## PDD Agentic Sync - Error` public comment must pass through terminal-noise and secret sanitization before posting. Remove real and caret-encoded CSI/ANSI sequences, cursor controls, control bytes, braille/Dingbat/box-drawing/spinner frames, auto-update/helper text, permission/footer hints, and cursor-concatenated garbage. Preserve an exact trusted provider-environment marker as its own full line. When present, add plain recovery guidance naming all concrete options: fix provider installation/auth/update state, switch provider, or use non-interactive configuration. Never include raw provider UI in the comment.
- All agentic-sync identification and dry-run-repair provider calls use `background_safe=True`; dry-run child environments also set `PDD_AGENTIC_BACKGROUND_SAFE=1`. At every dry-run boundary (initial child, repair provider, suggested command, validation aggregate, and final `run_agentic_sync` return), recognize only an allowlisted marker that occupies an exact full line, propagate it without basename or stage prefixes, skip further repair attempts, and let the public poster preserve that standalone line plus recovery guidance. Embedded/quoted/indented/extra-key marker text remains ordinary failure output.

